A Rust `Mutex` is a synchronized, thread-safe wrapper around a mutable data structure that ensures only one thread can access it at a time.
```rust
use std::sync::{Arc, Mutex};

fn main() {
    let data = Arc::new(Mutex::new(0));
    let mut guard = data.lock().unwrap();
    guard += 1;
}
```
This locks the `Mutex` to allow atomic increment of `data`.
